invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_x25519_base inverts its branch, so x25519_base runs the wide
  field, on the native 64x64->128 multiply, for every answer but
  WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME, a wiped direction's 0 and WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED among
  them, and the 16-word field on the decomposition for the one answer that
  states the multiply's timing. Every byte still comes out the same.
  bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into each copy and requires
  the wide field alone under the constant-time answer.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
        x25519_wide_base(out, scalar);
--- new
    if (!widemul_native(widemul)) {
        x25519_wide_base(out, scalar);
